    for item in receipts["members"].as_array().unwrap(){let root=if item["root"]=="raw"{RAW}else{R};let bytes=item["utf8"].as_str().unwrap().as_bytes();assert_eq!(item["length"],bytes.len());assert_eq!(item["sha256"],hash(bytes));assert_eq!(bytes,fs::read(Path::new(root).join(item["path"].as_str().unwrap())).unwrap());}
    let mut text=String::from("# Native joint-ring G2 query experiment\n\n**Rejected.** The primary32-worker G2 query is **60.24% slower than fresh OFF** and **49.79% slower than optimized FROZEN**. Peak query-process RSS rises from34.25MiB to145.75MiB. The fixed candidate is closed without a fullSDK trial or adoption. Production and accepted proof timings remain unchanged.\n\nThe [work screen](../2026-11-06-g2-joint-ring-screen176/README.md) and [queue/tree census](../2026-11-06-g2-joint-ring-census176/README.md) found fewer modeled additions. Native counters confirm fewer instructions, but extra memory traffic, construction and merging overwhelm that saving on this machine. These observations do not establish a RAM-capacity limit or isolate one cause.\n\n## Complete-query measurements\n\nRyzen9950X,16physical/32logicalCPUs. B queries for1×2 and2×2 at1/16/32workers; unchanged primary A32 negative control. Solo pinsCPU2; wider pools pin0..workers−1 with512KiB worker stacks. Every process primes3times, times17queries, then checks once more. Table times are medians of15process medians. Ratios and bounds use matched block observations and need not equal ratios of displayed times.\n\n|Query / workers|FROZEN ms|OFF ms|ON ms|ON/OFF ratio [bounds]|Wins/15|OFF/ON maxRSS MiB|\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---|---:|---:|\n");
