    text.push_str("\nThe two-shape32-worker aggregate is ON/OFF1.630628 [1.609504,1.670860],0/15wins; ON/FROZEN1.510786 [1.490109,1.526090],0/15wins. All gain conditions fail. Nonregression also fails. OFF/FROZEN calibration fails in all four wide B contexts: fresh OFF is about6–8% faster than the optimized frozen API control. That discrepancy remains unresolved; no accepted-build improvement or causal source change is inferred from it. The candidate is slower than both controls in those contexts, so calibration failure does not change the engineering rejection. All observations remain in the analysis.\n\nPredeclared15rotated/reversed blocks, all7contexts and3variants. Individual median intervals use sorted ranks4–12/15, nominal96.484375% marginal coverage under exchangeable independent blocks, not familywise. All OFF/FROZEN intervals must fit[1/1.03,1.03]; every ON/OFF and ON/FROZEN upper ratio≤1.02. PrimaryB32 and the equal-log primaryB32/2×2B32 aggregate each require upper<1 and≥10/15wins against both controls. No gain floor, exclusions, extensions, changed margins, subset selection or parameter/layout/worker reroll. [Full protocol](artifacts/protocol.md).\n\nEvery query includes original grouping, candidate admission/preparation/digit allocation, fills, merges, coordinate trees, drop and output normalization. Scalar reset copies remain inside every B timer. Parsing and worker construction are outside. Every output matches inherited complete Arkworks fixture hashes; every point input remains unchanged. Actual2×2 queries include their admitted grouping; the earlier raw2×2 model did not represent that runtime population. Peak RSS includes loading, primes and allocator retention, not minimumRAM, full-proof memory or pressure/concurrency qualification.\n\n## Counters and automatic profiles\n\nAll315latency processes finish before6FIFO-gated four-event PMUpanels, then6separate fixed16Mcycles:u profiles. Each diagnostic measures200queries after3excluded primes. Ownership/event/loss/decode checks run after every capture is terminal. No owned build, hash, archive, analyzer, verifier or second workload overlaps recording.\n\n|Diagnostic|Instructions/query M|Cycles/query M|Generic cache misses/query M|Branch misses/query M|IPC|\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n");
    for(name,c)in a["counters"].as_object().unwrap(){assert_eq!(c["qualified"],true);let e=|name:&str|c["events"][name]["per_query"].as_f64().unwrap();writeln!(text,"|{name}|{:.3}|{:.3}|{:.3}|{:.3}|{:.3}|",e("instructions:u")/1e6,e("cycles:u")/1e6,e("cache-misses:u")/1e6,e("branch-misses:u")/1e6,e("instructions:u")/e("cycles:u")).unwrap();}
    text.push_str("\nAll stat events run100%. Primary32 instructions decrease about6%, while user cycles increase66% and generic cache misses increase3.36×. Median minor faults/query increase86.7→790.1; median systemCPU/query increases1.86→5.56ms, and totalCPU/query69.88→113.76ms. Counter panels are separate observations, not paired latency estimates. Generic cache events do not identify a cache level; minor faults are not disk reads and do not establish swapping or insufficient installed RAM. User-cycle counts aggregate logical threads, including SMT.\n\n|Profile|Samples|Unknown share|Qualified|\n|---|---:|---:|---|\n");
