    text.push_str("\nThe6profiles contain28,375samples, zero lost records and verified actual PID, workerTID/CPU pairs,16Mperiod and executableMMAP bindings. Primary32 ON flat samples include10.23% in Window::new,11.57% in the bucket-merge iterator wrapper and12.15% in the owned G2 prefix kernel; OFF instead spends41.07% in the borrowed G2 kernel. Shares include inlining and surrounding work, are not exclusive critical-path time or removable latency, and absolute event-period coverage is not validated. [Full symbols](artifacts/symbols.json).\n\n## Implementation and memory\n\nFixed radix128,19ring windows,2original point-range parts. Six scalar units map to2,731integer representatives in3signed planes,8,193G2bucket slots perpart. A64KiB circuit-independent integer residue map and fixed signed-axis routing live in read-only executable data. No per-key point table, transformed proving-key copy or retained duplicate plan is built. Codes occupy38bytes perinput scalar. Merge parts, apply φ to completed unit planes, merge representatives, then reuse signed coordinate grouping and128-entry padded weighted trees. Existing field representation, scalar splitting, point arithmetic, borrowed streaming queues and complete exceptional paths stay unchanged.\n\nBuckets need1MiB of coordinate payload perpart versus256KiB originally. More live planes, owned merge operands, initialization, axes and allocation are costs beyond generic-add counts. The profiles and PMUdata are consistent with that broader working set and movement cost, but do not isolate a memory-level bottleneck. This experiment does not select a smaller-plane or different-width rescue.\n\nBefore allocating candidate scratch, a checked optional reservation covers all19×2suspended parent outputs, indexed-top inputs/results, code storage, axis outputs, routing data and worst nonforking leaf scratch perworker, on top of existing proof forecasts. It does not bound suspended parents by worker count. Overflow, unsupported geometry/kernel or denied admission returns the original borrowed fallback before changing inputs. This conservative reservation is not actual allocated memory or a pressure guarantee. The inherited driver's retained_payload_bytes field records this reservation; it is not a measured retained allocation.\n\n## Native qualification and preserved preflight failure\n\nThe initial private hook covered only the nongrouped return. It passed OFF125/ON129core tests and all21complete-output preflight processes. Its activation checker then stopped before any latency block because grouped2×2 bypassed that hook. No speed decision used those preflight clocks. The original source, libraries, executables,21caller receipts and failed checker remain preserved.\n\nThe successor moves the same optional hook into the shared g2_phi entry after its existing geometry guard, covering eligible raw and grouped inputs. No arithmetic, table, width, part count, resource formula or performance threshold changes. A new8192-input/1536-class generator test requires grouped route314 through the complete query API at1/4/16/32workers, with original inputs preserved. The changed integration passes OFF125/ON130unfiltered core tests on its first native workflow, plus coherent library builds/freeze. Four earlier native cases are applied to the changed integration, with one new case; these are5new cases total, not9independent tests. Field qualification is inherited without rerun because all field/kernel bodies remain exact.\n\nBoth snapshots contain178files;171of176 originals are byte-exact and all176 original bytes recover by reversing5diagnostic/dispatch/visibility edits. Generated constants are byte-identical across attempts and are not regenerated. Every new core links with its own coherent field/dependencies; original and fresh core/field libraries are not mixed. Final frozen, OFF and ON query drivers have exact same source and verified O/native/fatLTO/CGU1 flags. The frozen control is the existing optimized query-release0ba4build; earlier unoptimized coalesce/late-M3 executables are excluded.\n\nSeven unchanged frozen preflight receipts are reused with exact binary/input/command/stream bindings. New artifacts receive14first preflights; all required B ON routes activate314. The372-step shared workflow records341new callers plus7reused preflights,348qualified rows. It checks9,168query invocations including35reused;9,133are new shared calls. The initial raw attempt adds105calls, so9,238calls execute across the two native attempts without counting reused data twice. These are component queries, not SDK proofs.\n\nInitial helper failures are retained: a missing formatter-trait import in constant generation, a moved-path borrow in compiler pinning, and an unsupported per-link environment field rejected before any link. Narrow repairs precede each first successful execution; no successful native test/library/freeze, link or capture is repeated for bookkeeping. Initial schema/source/log copies and the compiler-environment revision remain in receipts. The closeout reviewer initially normalizes omitted link flags as empty instead of the tool's default optimized flags; correcting that bookkeeping check reuses every existing result.\n\nIndependent closeout checks1,793pin occurrences,409successful workflow commands and1preserved failing activation checker; both source recoveries, native suites, coherent libraries, final link flags, every query/oracle/activation/affinity receipt, raw PMUcounts and exact profileworkerCPU bindings pass. It independently reconstructs all17-query process medians, paired ranks, gain/nonregression/calibration gates and RSS/CPU summaries. [Review](artifacts/review.json). No native result is adopted and no successful recording is rerun.\n\n## Accepted proof comparison, inherited\n\nNo new fullSDK latency, serialized proof or Gnark export. Canonical distinct-proof ledger remains30,708. No new AWS/Aeglos, ARM/mobile/TEE,250/4999, pressure/swap/minimumRAM or concurrent-throughput result. The all-eight CPU10× goal remains active and unmet0/8. Accepted32-worker local proof timings and supplied historical M5 CPU/Metal references follow. They are not measurements from this query trial.\n\n|Shape|Accepted ms|M5 CPU ms|M5 Metal ms|CPU/local|Metal/local|CPU10× target ms|\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n");
    let manifest=read("/home/ubuntu/src/zk-tools/zopro/docs/benchmarks/2026-10-30-g2-vector-sign-adoption176/artifacts/production-source-manifest.json");
    for key in["1x2","2x2","4x2","8x2","12x2","16x2","24x2","merge-24x1"]{let v=&manifest["m5"][key];assert_eq!(v["goal10x"],false);let f=|k:&str|v[k].as_f64().unwrap();writeln!(text,"|{key}|{:.6}|{:.0}|{:.0}|{:.3}×|{:.3}×|{:.1}|",f("accepted_ms"),f("cpu_reference_ms"),f("metal_reference_ms"),f("cpu_speedup"),f("metal_speedup"),f("required_ms_for_CPU10x")).unwrap();}
